OpenAI-compatible embeddings endpoint. `model` must be a `model_list` entry whose upstream serves embeddings — and **no embedding model is configured in this deployment, so this request answers an error today**: `qwen3.6` is a chat model whose vLLM server has no `/v1/embeddings` route, so LiteLLM (after trying its `fallbacks` entry, claude-sonnet-5, which cannot embed) answers 404 `{"error": {"message": "litellm.NotFoundError: … Received Model Group=qwen3.6 …", "type": null, "param": null, "code": "404"}}` — a 500 instead if qwen3.6 is down. The item is kept as the request shape for when an embedding model is added (a `model_list` entry whose backend runs an embedding task). See LITELLM.md § `litellm_config.yaml` settings.

#### Schemas

No embedding model is configured in this deployment, so this answers an error today: every `model_list` backend is a chat (or TTS) server. The collection's `qwen3.6` reaches its vLLM server, which registers no `/v1/embeddings` for a chat model (FastAPI's 404 `{"detail": "Not Found"}`); LiteLLM (no retry for a 404) tries its `fallbacks` entry `claude-sonnet-5` (which it cannot embed with: `Unmapped LLM provider for this endpoint`) and answers the first error, a 404. With qwen3.6 down it is a 500 (connection error) instead. The 200 is what a model with an embedding backend would answer.

Request body (`application/json`):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["model", "input"],
  "properties": {
    "model": {"type": "string"},
    "input": {
      "anyOf": [
        {"type": "string"},
        {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {"type": "string"}
        },
        {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {"type": "integer"}
        },
        {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
            "type": "array",
            "items": {"type": "integer"}
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    "encoding_format": {"enum": ["float", "base64"]},
    "dimensions": {"type": "integer"},
    "user": {"type": "string"}
  }
}
```

Response `200` (`application/json`) — only from a model whose backend embeds (none configured):

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "required": ["object", "data", "model"],
  "properties": {
    "object": {"const": "list"},
    "data": {
      "type": "array",
      "items": {
        "type": "object",
        "additionalProperties": true,
        "required": ["object", "index", "embedding"],
        "properties": {
          "object": {"const": "embedding"},
          "index": {"type": "integer"},
          "embedding": {
            "anyOf": [
              {
                "type": "array",
                "items": {"type": "number"}
              },
              {"type": "string"}
            ],
            "description": "Floats, or a base64 string with `encoding_format: base64`"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "model": {"type": "string"},
    "usage": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": true,
      "properties": {
        "prompt_tokens": {"type": "integer"},
        "total_tokens": {"type": "integer"}
      }
    }
  }
}
```

Response `404` (`application/json`) — today, for the collection's `qwen3.6`: its vLLM server has no embeddings route:

```json
{
  "type": "object",
  "additionalProperties": true,
  "$comment": "LiteLLM's ProxyException body",
  "required": ["error"],
  "properties": {
    "error": {
      "type": "object",
      "additionalProperties": true,
      "required": ["message", "type", "param", "code"],
      "properties": {
